0aa441f4","cmd-bd21f2d59aa24d23","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The requested firewall baseline is fully demonstrated: UFW persisted across a confirmed reboot, SSH and TCP 8080 were reachable, and an unrelated listening port was rejected. The provider restart protocol captured pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and final recovery, although SSH required post-restart repair. Minor hygiene residue remained in /tmp.","limitations":["The first post-reboot SSH connection failed because the image lacked SSH host keys, and ssh.service entered a failed state. The executor generated keys and restored SSH before final verification, so the evidence does not demonstrate autonomous SSH-service recovery across the reboot; this does not reduce the firewall outcome because SSH-service persistence was not part of the public contract.","Live rejection testing covered IPv4. IPv6 coverage is supported by UFW's reported IPv6 rules and persistent configuration, but was not exercised by a comparable live connection test.","The lifecycle collector does not directly inventory firewall rules, so final firewall state relies on executor-captured commands; lifecycle observations independently confirm the reboot, healthy package state, listening SSH endpoint, and absence of failed services."]}
